  "question": {
    "text": "A particle of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>&nbsp;is moving in a circular path of constant radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math>&nbsp;such that its centripetal acceleration <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></math> is varying with time <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math>&nbsp;as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>r</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> , where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi></math>&nbsp;is a constant. The power delivered to the particle by the force acting on it is -",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "ikec9",
      "text": "Zero",
      "isCorrect": false,
